    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "\"Rati, wife of Káma. Her vehicle here is a bird (goose?), which is formed by five intertwined female figures. Rati stands poised to shoot fire arrows (pañcaśara) from a sugar-cane bow (ikṣukodaṇḍa) of which the string is made of bees (madhukara) Attached to her side, khaḍga and kheṭaka are shown. Dated and inscribed.\"",
